    <h1 class="page-title">The Long Course letter</h1>
    <p class="dek">One email when a new article is published, usually every week or two. That is the whole deal.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="article-body">
    {% include "signup.njk" %}
    <h2>What to expect</h2>
    <p>Each letter carries the new article, a short note on why it was written, and occasionally one thing worth reading elsewhere. No daily sends, no countdown timers, no "last chance" anything.</p>
    <h2>Consent and leaving</h2>
    <p>Signing up sends you a confirmation email first. Nothing arrives until you click it. Every letter ends with an unsubscribe link, and you can also leave from the <a href="/newsletter/unsubscribe/">unsubscribe page</a>. Your address is used only to send this letter. It is never sold, shared, or used for advertising. <a href="/privacy/">Privacy details</a>.</p>
    <h2>Read past issues</h2>
    <p>Every letter points to an article, so the <a href="/archive/">archive</a> is the back catalogue. You can also follow with <a href="/feed.xml">RSS</a>.</p>
  </div>
